% M7-T33 / D-0156: an all_different REGIN conflict under a decision now LEARNS, and the
% holes it read are cited through their remover's facts.
%
% Deciding k <= 2 (k = 2) makes the three int_ne punch the hole 2 in x1, x2, x3, each with
% the tail k <= 2. Every window is still 1..3, so stage 1 sees a Hall interval with nothing
% to push, and the matching over {1, 3} cannot saturate three variables. Until M7-T33 that
% conflict carried Reason.none; now its facts are the members' bounds (all declared here)
% and the remover's facts of every hole the derivation cancels -- k <= 2, listed once --
% and the derivation is written ahead of the line. k = 3 then moves every upper bound to
% 2, a stage-1 conflict; k = 4 is SAT.
%
% SAT (D-0053). test_prop.ml's M7-T33 lanes pin the Regin conflict line and refuse it
% standalone and without its pol.
var 2..4: k :: output_var;
var 1..3: x1 :: output_var;
var 1..3: x2 :: output_var;
var 1..3: x3 :: output_var;
constraint int_ne(x1,k);
constraint int_ne(x2,k);
constraint int_ne(x3,k);
constraint all_different_int([x1,x2,x3]);
solve :: int_search([k,x1,x2,x3], input_order, indomain_min, complete) satisfy;
